  "description": "Three records are read and displayed normally and the fourth READ reports '04', a record whose length disagrees with the copybook. Ten lines: the opening banner, six record lines, then the three failure lines. This case pins the ORDER that the two other read cases cannot - the error lines follow every line the successful reads already produced, because 1000-XREFFILE-GET-NEXT is performed inside the loop at :76 rather than before it - and it pins that '04' is fatal here. '04' is a status this program never names: :94 tests only '00' and :98 only '10', so everything else falls to :101. There is no END OF EXECUTION line, because :113 abends before :83 and :85 are reached.",
